From: DuckHTS maintainers
Subject: Load the compressed index of a CRAM without records

htslib 1.25 reads the .crai through BGZF and rejects an index that
decompresses to nothing. samtools index writes such an index, a gzip stream
of no bytes, for a CRAM without records, so 1.25 cannot load the index it
wrote. Reject only an uncompressed empty file, as before 1.25. The
empty-file check came with htslib PR 2085 (BGZF reading of the .crai).

diff --git a/cram/cram_index.c b/cram/cram_index.c
index 719a778..ad759eb 100644
--- a/cram/cram_index.c
+++ b/cram/cram_index.c
@@ -232,7 +232,8 @@ int cram_index_load(cram_fd *fd, const char *fn, const char *fn_idx) {
             goto fail;
     }
 
-    if (len < 0 || kstr.l < 1)
+    // A compressed index of a CRAM without records holds no entries.
+    if (len < 0 || (kstr.l < 1 && bgzf_compression(fp) == no_compression))
         goto fail;
 
     int ret = bgzf_close(fp);
